This is the Python String Methods list. Here is a simple way to understand the important ones:

Method	Simple Meaning	Example	Output

capitalize()	- First letter uppercase	"hello".capitalize()	Hello
casefold()	Convert to lowercase	"HELLO".casefold()	hello
center()	Put string in center	"Hi".center(6)	 Hi 
count()	Count occurrences	"banana".count("a")	3
endswith()	Check ending	"hello".endswith("o")	True
find()	Find position	"hello".find("l")	2
index()	Find position	"hello".index("e")	1
isalnum()	Only letters/numbers	"abc123".isalnum()	True
isalpha()	Only alphabets	"Hello".isalpha()	True
isdigit()	Only digits	"123".isdigit()	True
islower()	All lowercase	"hello".islower()	True
isupper()	All uppercase	"HELLO".isupper()	True
isspace()	Only spaces	"   ".isspace()	True
lower()	Convert lowercase	"HELLO".lower()	hello
upper()	Convert uppercase	"hello".upper()	HELLO
strip()	Remove spaces at both ends	" hi ".strip()	hi
lstrip()	Remove left spaces	" hi".lstrip()	hi
rstrip()	Remove right spaces	"hi ".rstrip()	hi
replace()	Replace text	"Hello".replace("H","Y")	Yello
split()	Convert string to list	"a,b,c".split(",")	['a','b','c']
join()	Join list elements	"-".join(["a","b"])	a-b
startswith()	Check beginning	"hello".startswith("h")	True
title()	First letter of each word uppercase	"hello world".title()	Hello World
swapcase()	Upper ↔ lower	"Hello".swapcase()	hELLO
zfill()	Add zeros at beginning	"25".zfill(5)	00025


⭐ Most important for beginners

Focus on these first:

1. upper() / lower()

name = "Dhanenthira"

print(name.upper())
print(name.lower())

2. replace()

text = "I like Java"
print(text.replace("Java", "Python"))

3. split()

text = "apple,banana,mango"
print(text.split(","))

4. strip()

text = "   hello   "
print(text.strip())

5. find()

text = "Hello Python"
print(text.find("Python"))

6. count()

text = "banana"
print(text.count("a"))

7. isalpha() / isdigit() / isalnum()

print("Hello".isalpha())   # True
print("123".isdigit())     # True
print("Hello123".isalnum()) # True
